-- Counting red objects over a TEN-field product scene of all-discrete CLEVR
-- objects (97 values each), by a flat `+` chain -- the order-independent
-- per-object scene of experiments_nest clevr-per-object-encoder. Draw sinking
-- splits the draw per field, so each summand is its own dense enumeration of
-- one slot. Two things made the query cost C(10, k) at count k (46 s at k = 5,
-- OOM at batch 64; task product-scene-discrete-count-enumerates-slot-patterns):
-- the summands all read the symbol parameter `s`, which the decomposability
-- gate counted as a shared latent, so no level of the chain was tabulated and
-- every split re-descended into its prefix; and each slot's `hit sc_oi`
-- re-enumerated the already-enumerated slot value, 97x per cell. Now the chain
-- is a materialized Poisson-binomial DP, linear in the slot count.
--
-- ORACLE: Poisson-binomial over q_i = P(Obj_i) * P(Red_i), slot i's logits
-- [Nil, Obj | Cube, Sphere, Cylinder | Small, Large | 8 colours | Rubber, Metal].
data Shape = Cube | Sphere | Cylinder
data Size = Small | Large
data Color = Red | Blue | Green | Yellow | Grey | Brown | Cyan | Purple
data Material = Rubber | Metal
data Object = Nil | Obj shape::Shape, size::Size, color::Color, material::Material
data Scene = Scene o1::Object, o2::Object, o3::Object, o4::Object, o5::Object, o6::Object, o7::Object, o8::Object, o9::Object, o10::Object
neural readScene :: (Symbol -> Scene)
hit o = if isNil o then 0 else (if isRed (color o) then 1 else 0)
main s = draw sc = readScene s in hit (o1 sc) + hit (o2 sc) + hit (o3 sc) + hit (o4 sc) + hit (o5 sc) + hit (o6 sc) + hit (o7 sc) + hit (o8 sc) + hit (o9 sc) + hit (o10 sc)
